Relevant columns and why they matter  
• event_date: restrict the scan to 1‑30 Nov 2020 (value is in the form YYYYMMDD).  
• event_name: keep only rows whose value = 'purchase'.  
• ecommerce.purchase_revenue_in_usd: metric to aggregate (only keep rows where it is not NULL).  
• event_params (ARRAY of key / value RECORDS): un‑nest to find the element whose key = 'ga_session_id'; the corresponding value.int_value is the session identifier.  
• user_pseudo_id: the visitor id we have to report on.  

Typical filter clauses  
event_date BETWEEN '20201101' AND '20201130'  
event_name = 'purchase'  
ecommerce.purchase_revenue_in_usd IS NOT NULL  
ep.key = 'ga_session_id' (after UNNEST event_params AS ep)  

