Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and why they matter  
• event_date: restrict the scan to 1‑30 Nov 2020 (value is in the form YYYYMMDD).  
• event_name: keep only rows whose value = 'purchase'.  
• ecommerce.purchase_revenue_in_usd: metric to aggregate (only keep rows where it is not NULL).  
• event_params (ARRAY of key / value RECORDS): un‑nest to find the element whose key = 'ga_session_id'; the corresponding value.int_value is the session identifier.  
• user_pseudo_id: the visitor id we have to report on.  

Typical filter clauses  
event_date BETWEEN '20201101' AND '20201130'  
event_name = 'purchase'  
ecommerce.purchase_revenue_in_usd IS NOT NULL  
ep.key = 'ga_session_id' (after UNNEST event_params AS ep)  

Below are 10 exploratory → increasingly complete queries (all capped with LIMIT 20).  

```sql
--Description: 1) Peek at any rows for 1 Nov 2020.
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20201101`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) Show purchase events with a non‑null USD revenue on 1 Nov 2020.
SELECT user_pseudo_id,
       event_date,
       ecommerce.purchase_revenue_in_usd
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20201101`
WHERE event_name = 'purchase'
  AND ecommerce.purchase_revenue_in_usd IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Extract the ga_session_id from the nested event_params array (1 Nov 2020 only).
SELECT user_pseudo_id,
       ep.value.int_value AS ga_session_id,
       ecommerce.purchase_revenue_in_usd
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20201101`,
     UNNEST(event_params) AS ep
WHERE event_name = 'purchase'
  AND ep.key = 'ga_session_id'
  AND ecommerce.purchase_revenue_in_usd IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Revenue summed per user & session on 1 Nov 2020.
SELECT user_pseudo_id,
       ga_session_id,
       SUM(ecommerce.purchase_revenue_in_usd) AS session_revenue_usd
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20201101`,
     UNNEST(event_params) AS ep
WHERE event_name = 'purchase'
  AND ep.key = 'ga_session_id'
  AND ecommerce.purchase_revenue_in_usd IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY user_pseudo_id, ga_session_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Sample purchase rows from every November table (using wildcard).
SELECT DISTINCT _TABLE_SUFFIX AS tbl_suffix,
       user_pseudo_id,
       ecommerce.purchase_revenue_in_usd
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_202011*`
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20201101' AND '20201130'
  AND event_name = 'purchase'
  AND ecommerce.purchase_revenue_in_usd IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Count purchase sessions per user across 1‑30 Nov 2020.
SELECT user_pseudo_id,
       COUNT(DISTINCT ga_session_id) AS purchase_sessions
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_202011*`,
     UNNEST(event_params) AS ep
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20201101' AND '20201130'
  AND event_name = 'purchase'
  AND ecommerce.purchase_revenue_in_usd IS NOT NULL
  AND ep.key = 'ga_session_id'
GROUP BY user_pseudo_id
HAVING purchase_sessions > 1
ORDER BY purchase_sessions DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Revenue per user & session across the whole month.
SELECT user_pseudo_id,
       ga_session_id,
       SUM(ecommerce.purchase_revenue_in_usd) AS session_revenue_usd
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_202011*`,
     UNNEST(event_params) AS ep
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20201101' AND '20201130'
  AND event_name = 'purchase'
  AND ecommerce.purchase_revenue_in_usd IS NOT NULL
  AND ep.key = 'ga_session_id'
GROUP BY user_pseudo_id, ga_session_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Average purchase revenue per session for every user (all Nov tables), no session‑count filter yet.
SELECT user_pseudo_id,
       AVG(session_revenue_usd) AS avg_rev_per_session
FROM (
    SELECT user_pseudo_id,
           ga_session_id,
           SUM(ecommerce.purchase_revenue_in_usd) AS session_revenue_usd
    FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_202011*`,
         UNNEST(event_params) AS ep
    WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20201101' AND '20201130'
      AND event_name = 'purchase'
      AND ecommerce.purchase_revenue_in_usd IS NOT NULL
      AND ep.key = 'ga_session_id'
    GROUP BY user_pseudo_id, ga_session_id )
GROUP BY user_pseudo_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) FINAL LOGIC (users with >1 purchase session) – average revenue per purchase session.
SELECT user_pseudo_id,
       AVG(session_revenue_usd) AS avg_purchase_rev_per_session
FROM (
    SELECT user_pseudo_id,
           ga_session_id,
           SUM(ecommerce.purchase_revenue_in_usd) AS session_revenue_usd
    FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_202011*`,
         UNNEST(event_params) AS ep
    WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20201101' AND '20201130'
      AND event_name = 'purchase'
      AND ecommerce.purchase_revenue_in_usd IS NOT NULL
      AND ep.key = 'ga_session_id'
    GROUP BY user_pseudo_id, ga_session_id )
GROUP BY user_pseudo_id
HAVING COUNT(*) > 1
ORDER BY avg_purchase_rev_per_session DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 10) Same as #9 but rewritten with CTEs for clarity.
WITH purchase_events AS (
  SELECT user_pseudo_id,
         ep.value.int_value AS ga_session_id,
         ecommerce.purchase_revenue_in_usd
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_202011*`,
       UNNEST(event_params) AS ep
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20201101' AND '20201130'
    AND event_name = 'purchase'
    AND ecommerce.purchase_revenue_in_usd IS NOT NULL
    AND ep.key = 'ga_session_id'
),
session_level AS (
  SELECT user_pseudo_id,
         ga_session_id,
         SUM(ecommerce.purchase_revenue_in_usd) AS session_revenue_usd
  FROM purchase_events
  GROUP BY user_pseudo_id, ga_session_id
)
SELECT user_pseudo_id,
       AVG(session_revenue_usd) AS avg_purchase_rev_per_session
FROM session_level
GROUP BY user_pseudo_id
HAVING COUNT(*) > 1
ORDER BY avg_purchase_rev_per_session DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

